{
    "$comment": "Scoop manifest for the dsscp compiler, rendered by packaging/render.py. The release tarball is a PREFIX TREE produced by `cmake --install` (bin/, lib/, share/) — see cmake/DssInstall.cmake, the single owner of what ships. Scoop extracts it whole into the app directory and shims `bin\\dsscp.exe`, so the exe keeps its relative hop to share\\dss-code-prime\\<version>\\dss-config, which is how it finds the descriptors that resolve `#include <stdio.h>`. A shim launches the real exe in place rather than copying it, so the hop survives. Still depends on the queued dss-code-prime -> dsscp binary rename.",
